- ### Pattern matching
+ ### Coincidencia de patrones

- The `h"…"` interpolator is also a pattern. A literal pattern matches an equal node, whether
- the value is that node, or a fragment which contains only it. It is checked as real HTML,
- against the structure of the nodes, not against the source text, so a pattern which is
- written with closing tags matches input which was written without them:
+ El interpolador `h"…"` es también un patrón. Un patrón literal coincide con un nodo igual, tanto
+ si el valor es ese nodo como si es un fragmento que solo lo contiene a él. Se comprueba como HTML
+ real, contra la estructura de los nodos, no contra el texto fuente, así que un patrón que se
+ escribe con etiquetas de cierre coincide con una entrada que se escribió sin ellas:

= written with closing tags matches input which was written without them:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val html = h"<li>two</li>"
+ val html = h"<li>two</li>"

- val matched = html match
+ val matched = html match

-   case h"<li>one</li>" => 1
+   case h"<li>one</li>" => 1

-   case h"<li>two</li>" => 2
+   case h"<li>two</li>" => 2

-   case _               => 0
+   case _               => 0

=   case _               => 0
- ```
+ ```

- Substitutions bind the pieces which a pattern captures. An `<li>` may hold text or
- elements, so a captured body is itself `Html`, which is matched in turn:
+ Las sustituciones ligan las piezas que captura un patrón. Un `<li>` puede contener texto o
+ elementos, así que un cuerpo capturado es a su vez `Html`, que se compara a su vez con patrones:

= elements, so a captured body is itself `Html`, which is matched in turn:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val nested = html match
+ val nested = html match

-   case h"<li>$value</li>" => value match
+   case h"<li>$value</li>" => value match

-     case Html.Text("one") => 1
+     case Html.Text("one") => 1

-     case Html.Text("two") => 2
+     case Html.Text("two") => 2

-     case _                => 0
+     case _                => 0

-   case _                  => 0
+   case _                  => 0

=   case _                  => 0
- ```
+ ```

=   case _                  => 0
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

=   case _                  => 0
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

=   case _                  => 0
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(matched.show)
+ Out.println(matched.show)

- Out.println(nested.show)
+ Out.println(nested.show)

= Out.println(nested.show)
- ```
+ ```

- Attributes, comments and elements can be captured too:
+ También se pueden capturar atributos, comentarios y elementos:

= Attributes, comments and elements can be captured too:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Pattern
- column  Matches
- row  `h"<li>$value</li>"`  an `<li>`, binding its body as `Html`
- row  `h"<img src=$source>"`  an `<img>`, binding the value of `src`
- row  `h"<img $attributes>"`  an `<img>`, binding its attribute map
- row  `h"<$element>"`  any element, but no other kind of node
+ column  Patrón
+ column  Coincide con
+ row  `h"<li>$value</li>"`  un `<li>`, ligando su cuerpo como `Html`
+ row  `h"<img src=$source>"`  un `<img>`, ligando el valor de `src`
+ row  `h"<img $attributes>"`  un `<img>`, ligando su mapa de atributos
+ row  `h"<$element>"`  cualquier elemento, pero ninguna otra clase de nodo

= row  `h"<$element>"`  any element, but no other kind of node
- ```
+ ```

